Z||000002||California Kid||12-14-2001||08:40 PM||||At your age, and on a very tight budget (that you don't want to throw into a car), you forgot the best alternative, the Honda Accord. If you can find one with good service records (owner who took care of it), it won't unexpectedly eat a hole in your wallet. Then you can save for the things that really matter to you.<P>All the car's you mentioned are pretty nice, but I doubt that you'll find one that doesn't eat into your wallet.<P>Just my opinion.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||85ZainoGT||12-14-2001||08:44 PM||||I would go 86-88 fiero gt... I have an 87 and love it.. but if not that, then I would prolly go, ya, although I dont really like them, a 93 mustang gt...  or if you could get a supra/300zx turbo, Id go with that..<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ejayerik||12-14-2001||08:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by want a fiero:<BR><B> What car should i get, i turn 16 in 2 weeks.<BR>  1. 86-88 fiero gt<BR>  2.87-92 camaro z28<BR>  3.87-92 Pontiac firebird gta<BR>  4.90-92 nissan 300zx NA<BR>  5.88-92 toyota supra<BR>  6.88-93 mustang lx/gt 5.0<BR>i hade a 88 fiero 4cly and it was alot of fun to drive but took alot of work to keep up and i have a tight budget so i can not put alot of money in it just to keep it running</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lets see, The Fiero will be a lot of fun to drive, The Z28 will cost you a fortune on gas and insurance, The Firebird will also cost the same but is more fun than the Camaro, The 300ZX is a very fun car to drive but it will kill you if you want to upgrade parts. There are plenty out there but they are all overpriced. Plus, any 300 ZX you will find for less than 10 thousand, it will have high miles on it. The Supra is a good car but the older ones just can't keep up with the newer ones if your thinking ricer. Plus, the turbos really tear up those engines. The Rustang??? I wouldn't even try. Though they can be good cars, they will cost you billions to make it halfway reliable and fast. Just my opinion..lol<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pyric||12-14-2001||08:53 PM||||I agree.  Unfortunately the more power and potential a car has the more you have to spend on maintenance.<P>Not to mention the fact that if you have a faster car, you're more likely to do something stupid and wreck it.<P>Try to hotrod in a car with only 110HP.<P>Hell, I did that with my Nissan Sentra in college.  But if I totaled it I'd just be out $2000 (at the time).  And I could rebuild the engine for $180.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Try and rebuild anything bigger than a 4 for that.<P>I'm still driving that Sentra to work, which means I can do anything at any time to the Fiero without having to worry about being out a ride.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Just something to think about.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">   <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
