Z||000008||Old Lar||12-14-2001||10:24 PM||||Lets see you are 16, car insurance will cost a bundle for you to drive anything resembling a "sports car".<P>  Find a Honda Civic.<P>But if mommy and daddy are footing the bill, get anything they will pay for.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||12-14-2001||10:31 PM||||Good luck finding much of a Turbo supra or 300ZX for 5000$ or less. If you do it probably needs work done to it. Parts for most imports cost allot more then on American cars. If its your first car a V8 F-Body will probably end up killing you.<P>Any pre 88 fiero will be the cheapest to keep runing.<P>But maybe look into a economy car.||||reg||1
Z||000010||soup||12-15-2001||03:31 AM||||IM 17 and im not having any trouble affording my 87 GT... I love it, its got power, good on gas, and rather cheap to plate. Those other cars are going to cost a lot more than the fiero. Personally, I hated th fiero more than anything before I saw my first GT (Which happens to be the one i own :Þ ) but I fell in love with it. IMO if you allready like the Fiero, it will be your best bet. And if you ever need help fixing it you always have this awesome forum to look back on, the people here are way more helpful lthan any other forum I have seen for cars. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Springtyme||12-15-2001||07:55 AM||||I'm 18, I got my fiero when I was 17 and I'm not having any problems. It's cheap on gas, I love driving it, and so far I have't had any problems that couldn't be fixed in less than 20 bucks. I have 2 cars, my Beretta I pay $365 on for 6 months, and my Fiero I pay $369 for 6 months. I dunno why you have a problem... Everyone else can see the answer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Hehehehe. Just kidding about the last part, but seriously, a fiero would probably be the best way to go.||||reg||10
