Z||000015||Svyn||12-15-2001||11:52 AM||||I would check on insurance costs, in Maryland they group the Fiero with Corvette's and other high end sports cars. The insurance is quite a bit. I have put about 1k in parts on the fiero (tires, alt, misc parts), bought it for 1k and driven it well over 30k miles (non baby'd miles). Still gets 24mpg while being beaten within and inch of of its life daily. <BR>I would suggest getting a larger car if possible, just for the security if someone hits you...<P>------------------<BR>-Dale Clark<BR>86' Fiero SE<BR>99' Dodge Durango SLT+<BR>92' Ford ThunderBird SuperCoupe||||reg||1
Z||000016||LoW_KeY||12-15-2001||01:07 PM||||If you do go w/ the supra you better know how to work on it or know someone that knows something about the car.<P>I know around my area they won't touch a fiero.. but I wouldn't let them anyways got my dads friend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> but it depends will you be driving it in winter etc. all of those are really light cars and can be tricky to drive.<P>The only money I've had to put in my car to make it run better was a clutch.. other stuff I've put in to it was my choice.. tires, paint, new spoiler, interior stuff.<P>if ya wanna be different go with the fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> hehe.. but hey I do like the other cars too!<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||GTFiero1||12-15-2001||01:42 PM||||well i vote for a fiero. firebirds and Ta's are nice but the 80's ones need money to keep up (my brother had one, rattle trap. but if have the money to make it nice then they are cool) also foreign cars may be built pretty good but as they get older there reliablity goes down and costs a lot to get fixed (aka: my brother 1st car, Nissian sentra, that thing... if we needed a part that if it was an american car would cost us 20 bucks, cost us 200) <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
