Z||000020||Peachez||12-15-2001||08:11 PM||||Im 16, bought my 84 fiero when i was 15 and besides putting in an engine ive had nothing to repair that i couldn't do myself (headlight motors, wiring, etc.)  fieros are lightweight, saves you gas money, exotic, cheap parts, and just hella fun to drive.  my dad and brother have mustangs and i gotta say i get a little jealous when he starts that baby up but.... then i remember how much crap he's had to do to it and how much crap he's gunna have to do to it to make it drivable....but wait he's gunna spend all his money fixing his car....that he wont have gas money to drive it.  BWA HA HA HA.  I think that goes for the other gas guzzlers you mentioned.  (oh yeah and he had a firebird too, it didn't run for more than a month tops; bought it for 2700 bucks.... people around town wont even pay 700 for it.)  the fiero is very inexpensive, unless you go crazy with modifications (not that thats a bad thing :devil <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  and would be IMHO the best choice for a daily driver. Ash*<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_&_me2.jpg">  ||||reg||1
